#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Judged by a human: the side pane in the Claude Code desktop app.
cat <<'T'
In a project set up with `delegate init`, start two runs with `delegate run --background`
(one with a worker that streams steps, one that goes quiet past the stall threshold), then
open the delegate pane in the Claude Code desktop app and watch it for a minute.
Look for:
- each task with phase, worker, elapsed time and files changed; latest steps of running tasks
- it updates by itself; the stalled task stands out
- no tasks: it says so instead of looking broken
- right in light and dark mode
Pass if all hold.
T
exit 2
